@startuml
title Cleanux — TO-BE Component Architecture (Post-Migration)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "src/ (Dioxus Frontend)" #LightBlue {
  [pages/]
  [components/]
  [hooks/]
  [signals/]
}

package "src/domain/" #LightGreen {
  [entities/ — CleaningProfile, AutomationRecipe, HealthSnapshot, ...]
  [value_objects/ — ScanResult, JunkCategory, ...]
  [services/ — ProfileDomainService, AutomationDomainService, ...]
}

package "src/application/" #LightYellow {
  [services/ — CleaningApplicationService, ScanApplicationService, ...]
  [kas/ — KAS handler registry]
}

package "src/infrastructure/" #LightPink {
  [persistence/ — nosql_orm adapters]
  [cleanup/ — System cleanup executors]
  [monitoring/ — sysinfo adapters]
}

package "dioxus-shared" #Orange {
  [themes/]
  [ui/render_component.rs — DynamicRenderer]
  [algorithms/]
  [schema/ — SDUI schemas]
}

package "src-tauri/ (Tauri Backend Only)" #Gray {
  [Tauri commands — thin IPC bridge]
  [tauri_plugin_mcp_bridge]
  [No business logic here]
}

Dioxus Frontend --> domain
Dioxus Frontend --> application
Dioxus Frontend --> infrastructure
Dioxus Frontend --> dioxus-shared
application --> domain
infrastructure --> dioxus-shared
Tauri Backend --> dioxus-shared

note bottom of Tauri Backend
  Post-migration: Tauri is ONLY an IPC bridge
  All business logic moves to Dioxus frontend as DDD layers
end note
@enduml
